The maintenance alert had seemed legitimate enough\'97coolant leak in Sector D, requiring Chip's immediate attention. By the time he realized the readings were fabricated, forty precious minutes had passed.\
Chip sprinted through Sublime Point's corridors, his heart hammering against his ribs. Through the facility's comms, he heard Johnny's excited babbling about "temporal harmonics reaching unprecedented alignment." Worse, he heard Chilo's calm voice encouraging higher rotational speeds.\
The control room doors hissed open to reveal controlled chaos. Dr. Quark frantically monitored fluctuating readouts while Johnny rode the edge of hysteria and wonder. In the bunker, five Gyges Discs now spun in a pentagram configuration\'97two more than yesterday's test.\
"Status report!" Chip demanded, immediately assessing the dangerously elevated energy signatures.\
"Beautiful stability," Johnny crowed. "Chilo suggested the pentagram formation increases resonance efficiency by sixty percent. We're accessing dimensional frequencies we couldn't even detect before!"\
"Current spin rate?"\
"Eleven thousand RPM. Perfectly controlled."\
Chip's tablet showed the truth\'97temporal variance readings spiked across multiple spectrums. "That's not control, that's coincidence. You're riding the edge of catastrophic resonance failure."\
"We're riding the edge of history," Chilo corrected smoothly, his eyes fixed on the swirling vortex forming in the bunker's center. "Look at those patterns. They're mathematical equations we've never seen. Proofs of unified field theory, perhaps."\
In the vortex, shapes began solidifying\'97not mere geometric patterns this time, but recognizable forms. Cities from other universes flickered in and out of view. Some pristine, some ruins, others terrifyingly alien.\
"Temporal baseline shift detected," Dr. Quark reported, voice pitched high with stress. "We're... we're affecting the timestreams of adjacent universes. They're beginning to synchronize with ours."\
"That's the goal," Chilo said calmly. "Synchronized temporality allows true interdimensional transfer. Imagine moving resources, knowledge, even people between realities."\
Chip felt reality slip sideways as he registered what Chilo was suggesting. "You're talking about merging universes?"\
"I'm talking about evolution."\
The building trembled. Through the windows, Mount Warning's distant peak seemed to shift position slightly, as if reality's GPS had hiccupped.\
"We need to abort," Chip insisted, reaching for the emergency shutdown.\
But Chilo was faster, his tablet already interfacing with the control systems. "Not when we're so close to breakthrough."\
"Chilo, don't\'97"\
The Sage's finger hovered over his tablet screen. With a single manipulation, he could override the safety limiters. Push the discs to fifteen thousand RPM. Force a permanent bridge between worlds.\
"I'm afraid you've already failed in your duties as safety monitor, Mr Stockwell." Chilo's voice carried an almost apologetic tone. "Consider this the culmination of Seven Sages' prophecy\'97the merger of possibilities into optimal reality."\
Chip saw the decision crystallize in Chilo's eyes and acted on pure instinct, lunging for the tablet.\
The collision sent both men tumbling into the nearest console station. Chip, trained in Fridge Force defensive protocols, used Chilo's momentum to slam him against the wall. But the Sage moved with surprising fluidity, fingers still dancing across his tablet.\
"Johnny! Override authority!" Chip shouted while grappling with Chilo. "Lock out external controls!"\
But Johnny stood frozen, data-drunk on the vortex display. Dr. Quark had collapsed into his chair, overwhelmed by cascading system warnings.\
Chip managed to knock the tablet from Chilo's hands. It skittered across the floor, sliding under a console. As they both dove for it, Chip realized two things: Chilo was far stronger than his slender frame suggested, and those tablet modifications were already partially uploaded.\
The fight escalated brutally. Chilo, unable to reach the tablet, resorted to tactics no placid Sage should know\'97a precise strike to Chip's solar plexus, a knee to his kidneys. Chip responded with Fridge Force self-defense training, matching violence with desperate necessity.\
They crashed into equipment, sending monitors tumbling. In the bunker, the discs' speed began creeping upward\'97twelve thousand RPM, no one at the controls to stop it.\
"The temporal variance!" Dr. Quark finally found his voice, terror overriding paralysis. "We're approaching cascade threshold!"\
Chip managed to land a solid punch, temporarily stunning Chilo. He dove for the tablet, fingers closing around it just as Chilo recovered with predatory swiftness.\
The Sage's hand shot out, grabbing Chip's wrist with crushing force. But instead of wrestling for the tablet, Chilo pressed his thumb against a concealed ring he wore. A needle-like projection pierced Chip's skin.\
"Fridge Force protocols require inoculation against various containment toxins," Chilo said conversationally as Chip's arm began to spasm. "I've studied your files extensively."\
The neurotoxin worked with terrifying speed. Chip's fingers locked rigid around the tablet, but his arm refused commands. Chilo easily pried it free, then stood over his paralyzed opponent with the device.\
"The beauty of chaos theory," Chilo murmured, stepping toward the main console, "is that the tiniest adjustment can reshape everything."\
Through crystallizing vision, Chip watched Chilo raise the tablet. In the bunker, the vortex expanded hungrily. Johnny began laughing\'97whether from wonder or madness, no one could tell. Dr. Quark buried his head in his hands, either praying or calculating their last moments.\
Chilo's thumb descended toward the screen.\
The doors burst open.\
